BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20260629T233000Z
DTEND:20260630T013000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall
SUMMARY:Winston Choi\, piano
DESCRIPTION:Repertoire to be announcedAbout the Artist  Canadian pianist 
 Winston Choi is professor and program director of piano at Roosevelt Univ
 ersity's Chicago College of Performing Arts. Winner of France's Concours 
 International de Piano 20e siècle d'Orléans and laureate of the Honens 
 International Piano Competition\, he is internationally recognized for hi
 s bold interpretations of the standard repertoire and his unwavering comm
 itment to contemporary music. He appears worldwide as a soloist\, chamber
  musician\, and educator. Choi has performed concertos with numerous Nort
 h American and international orchestras\, including the Civic Orchestra o
 f Chicago\, Calgary Philharmonic\, Victoria Symphony\, l'Orchestre Nation
 al de Lille\, and Colombia's national orchestra. His solo recitals have b
 rought him to such major venues as Carnegie-Weill Recital Hall\, the Kenn
 edy Center\, and France's Salle Cortot. A prolific chamber musician\, he 
 tours widely as a member of Civitas Ensemble\, Duo Diorama (with violinis
 t MingHuan Xu)\, and Trio Diorama (with Xu and cellist Nick Photinos)\, a
 nd recently performed with Matthias Goerne at the Ravinia Festival. A pas
 sionate advocate for new music\, Choi has premiered and commissioned over
  100 works. His recordings include Elliott Carter's complete piano music\
 , Jacques Lenot's works (winner of the Grand Prix du Disque)\, and music 
 by Thomas Adès. He appears on such labels as BIS\, Cedille\, and Naxos\,
  and is a core member of Ensemble Dal Niente. He earned degrees from Indi
 ana and Northwestern Universities\, and studied with Menahem Pressler and
  Ursula Oppens. A dedicated pedagogue\, Choi is also in demand as a maste
 r class clinician and conference presenter\, sharing insights on phrasing
 \, technique\, and interpretation.
